Z||000019||ffindley||12-02-2001||07:37 AM||||Thumbs up to yellow!  Great choice.  Look at all the beautiful ones!<P>Only issue with yellow is that it needs to be well detailed to look really good.  Otherwise, dirt and dust dulls it.  It helps to detail the black so that it stands off against the yellow.<P>Also, it looks really good with a black & Brushed Aluminum interior.<P>Here is my formula, repainted this year in very close to Stock Talbot Yellow. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/front_1_small.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_1_small.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pass_side_top.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rear_close_small.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/black_interior_pass_small.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/all_open_driver_small.JPG"> ||||reg||14
